## Use the identity with sin θ = 1/4
The identity $\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta = 1$ links $\cos\theta$ and $\sin\theta$.
\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta &= 1
\cos^2\theta + \left(\frac{1}{4}\right)^2 &= 1
## Isolate cos²θ
\cos^2\theta + \frac{1}{16} &= 1
\cos^2\theta &= 1 - \frac{1}{16}
\cos^2\theta &= \frac{15}{16}
## Take the square root
$\theta$ is acute, so $\cos\theta$ is positive.
\cos\theta &= \sqrt{\frac{15}{16}}
\cos\theta &= \frac{\sqrt{15}}{4}
ANSWER: \cos\theta = \frac{\sqrt{15}}{4}

## Use the complement
'At least one' the same is the opposite of 'none the same'.
P(\text{at least one}) &= 1 - P(\text{none the same})
## Find P(none the same)
Last week's $2$ panels are fixed. 'None the same' means both new panels come from the other $126$.
P(\text{none the same}) &= \frac{\binom{126}{2}}{\binom{128}{2}}
&= \frac{126 \times 125}{128 \times 127}
&= \frac{7875}{8128}
## Subtract from 1
P(\text{at least one}) &= 1 - \frac{7875}{8128}
&= \frac{253}{8128}
&= 0.031
ANSWER: 0.031

## Set up a tan ratio in triangle POA
The angle at $A$ is $90^\circ$, so $PA = 12$ is adjacent to $70^\circ$ and $AO$ is opposite.
\tan 70^\circ &= \frac{|AO|}{12}
## Isolate |AO|
|AO| &= 12 \tan 70^\circ
## Evaluate and round to 1 decimal place
|AO| &= 32.96\ldots
|AO| &= 33.0 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: |AO| = 33.0 \text{ cm}

## (i) Probability of a token on one roll
A token comes from rolling a 5 or a 6, which is 2 faces out of 6.
P(\text{token}) &= \frac{2}{6}
&= \frac{1}{3}
## (ii) Write the probability of no token
A first token on turn 5 means turns 1 to 4 give nothing, then turn 5 gives a token.
P(\text{nothing}) &= 1 - \frac{1}{3}
&= \frac{2}{3}
## (ii) Multiply the five turns
P &= \left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^4 \times \frac{1}{3}
&= \frac{16}{81} \times \frac{1}{3}
&= \frac{16}{243}
ANSWER: \text{(i) } \frac{1}{3}, \quad \text{(ii) } \frac{16}{243}

## Split into the two cases
Each turn is a token with probability $\frac{1}{3}$ and no token with probability $\frac{2}{3}$. Use the binomial formula.
P(4 \text{ or more}) &= P(4) + P(5)
## Find P(4)
P(4) &= \binom{5}{4}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^4\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^1
&= 5 \times \frac{1}{81} \times \frac{2}{3}
&= \frac{10}{243}
## Find P(5)
P(5) &= \left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^5
&= \frac{1}{243}
## Add the two probabilities
P(4 \text{ or more}) &= \frac{10}{243} + \frac{1}{243}
&= \frac{11}{243}
ANSWER: \frac{11}{243}

## Describe the tree diagram
First roll: 1 to 4 (probability $\frac{2}{3}$) gives 0 tokens. A 5 or 6 (probability $\frac{1}{3}$) leads to the choice.
Take the token with probability $p$: 1 token. Roll again with probability $1 - p$.
Second roll: 1 to 4 (probability $\frac{2}{3}$) gives 0 tokens. A 5 or 6 (probability $\frac{1}{3}$) gives 4 tokens.
## Find the probability of getting 1 token
Roll a 5 or 6, then take the token.
P(1 \text{ token}) &= \frac{1}{3} \times p
&= \frac{p}{3}
## Find the probability of getting 4 tokens
Roll a 5 or 6, roll again, then roll another 5 or 6.
P(4 \text{ tokens}) &= \frac{1}{3} \times (1 - p) \times \frac{1}{3}
&= \frac{1 - p}{9}
## Form the expected value
Expected value is each number of tokens times its probability, added up.
E &= 1 \times \frac{p}{3} + 4 \times \frac{1 - p}{9}
&= \frac{3p}{9} + \frac{4 - 4p}{9}
&= \frac{3p + 4 - 4p}{9}
&= \frac{4 - p}{9}
ANSWER: \frac{4 - p}{9}

## Compare the expected value at the two extremes
The expected value is $\frac{4 - p}{9}$, which gets smaller as $p$ gets bigger.
p = 0: \quad E &= \frac{4 - 0}{9}
&= \frac{4}{9}
p = 1: \quad E &= \frac{4 - 1}{9}
&= \frac{3}{9}
## Say what the player should do
$p = 0$ means the player never takes the single token.
So after rolling a 5 or a 6, the player should always roll again.
ANSWER: \text{Roll again after a 5 or a 6}

## Identify a, b and c
Compare $3x^2 - 4x - 5 = 0$ with $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$.
a &= 3
b &= -4
c &= -5
## Write the quadratic formula
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
## Substitute a, b and c
x &= \frac{-(-4) \pm \sqrt{(-4)^2 - 4(3)(-5)}}{2(3)}
x &= \frac{4 \pm \sqrt{16 + 60}}{6}
x &= \frac{4 \pm \sqrt{76}}{6}
## Evaluate the + root
x &= \frac{4 + \sqrt{76}}{6}
x &= 2.119\ldots
x &= 2.12
## Evaluate the − root
x &= \frac{4 - \sqrt{76}}{6}
x &= -0.786\ldots
x &= -0.79
ANSWER: x = 2.12 \text{ or } x = -0.79
